<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.3.1: Dividing by Monomials</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01613</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.3.1: Dividing by Monomials</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f3922b57-7d19-41d8-b958-2b755e5ba48b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para id="para-00001">In this unit, remember to double click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge, if needed.</para>
<para id="para-00002">In this unit, remember to double click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge, if needed.</para>

<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    
    <para id="para-00003">Look at the division expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>54</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:msup><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>÷</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:msup><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
    
    <para id="para-00004">Rewrite the division expression as a fraction.</para>
    <para id="para-00005">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
  <para id="para-00006">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00007">Fraction form: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>54</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:msup><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:msup><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>

</solution></exercise>


<exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    
    <para id="para-00008">Since we have a monomial divided by a monomial, we can rewrite the fraction as a product of several fractions where the factors in the numerator and denominator “match.”</para>
    <para id="para-00009">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
  <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>54</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution></exercise>


<exercise id="exer-00003">
  <problem id="prob-00003">
    
    <para id="para-00012">Now we can simplify the fraction multiplication and use the Quotient Property to divide.</para>
    <para id="para-00013">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00003">
  <para id="para-00014">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00015"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>54</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>·</m:mi><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>
    
    So <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>54</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:msup><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>÷</m:mi><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:msup><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.
</para>

</solution></exercise>


<exercise id="exer-00004">
  <problem id="prob-00004">
    
    <para id="para-00016">For 4 - 6, divide a polynomial by a monomial. Divide each term of the polynomial by the monomial.</para>
    
    <para id="para-00017">Find the quotient: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>18</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>÷</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
    <para id="para-00018">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00004">
  <para id="para-00019">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00020"><emphasis>Step 1 -</emphasis> Rewrite as a fraction.</para>
  
  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>18</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00022"><emphasis>Step 2 -</emphasis> Divide each term by the divisor.</para>
  
  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>18</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>36</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00024"><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Simplify.</para>

</solution></exercise>


<exercise id="exer-00005">
  <problem id="prob-00005">
    
    <para id="para-00025">Find the qoutient: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>48</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>÷</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
    <para id="para-00026">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00005">
  <para id="para-00027">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution></exercise>


<exercise id="exer-00006">
  <problem id="prob-00006">
    
    <para id="para-00029">Find the quotient: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>72</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:msup><m:msup><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>45</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:msup><m:msup><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mi>÷</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:msup><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
    <para id="para-00030">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00006">
  <para id="para-00031">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution></exercise>
</section>
</content>
</document>